WEBVTT

00:15:26.689 --> 00:15:31.027
he wrote a story about model airplanes
I had never heard before,

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:34.397
even though he couldn't even
use his fingers at the time.

00:15:34.764 --> 00:15:37.934
I sent another, “Tell me about
the house you grew up in.”

00:15:37.934 --> 00:15:39.936
Then another, "How did you join the Navy?"

00:15:39.969 --> 00:15:41.804
"How did you meet Mom?"

00:15:41.838 --> 00:15:44.373
Until just this week,

00:15:44.407 --> 00:15:47.543
eight years after that first question,

00:15:47.577 --> 00:15:48.744
my dad,

00:15:48.778 --> 00:15:51.781
who never wrote anything
longer than a memo,

00:15:51.814 --> 00:15:56.752
completed a 65,000-word memoir.

00:15:57.820 --> 00:15:59.388
One question,

00:15:59.422 --> 00:16:00.957
one story,